; regression test for the same false-rejection bug as
; forall-intro-vocabulary-not-scoped.kurt, but for `pick` (exists-elim): a bare
; boolean proposition `P` first used inside the block, in a conclusion that doesn't
; depend on the witness at all, used to be wrongly rejected as if `P` were as scoped
; to the block as the witness `y` itself. See doc/kurt-soundness.md.
load logic
bool Q, P
arity Q 1
use exists x Q x
pick y with Q y
    use P
    P
true
;;; Proof checked.
